      "SectionPath": [
        "Knowledge Anywhere Deep Integration Functionality"
      ],
      "Text": "The LinkedIn Learning and Knowledge Anywhere integration involves the following requirements:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Knowledge Anywhere Deep Integration Functionality",
      "Anchor": "knowledge-anywhere-deep-integration-functionality",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Knowledge Anywhere Deep Integration Functionality"
      ],
      "Text": "An active Knowledge Anywhere LMS instance\n\nAn active LinkedIn Learning account\n\nAdmin access to LinkedIn Learning\n\nAdmin privileges to your Knowledge Anywhere LMS instance",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Integration Overview",
      "Anchor": "integration-overview",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Integration Overview"
      ],
      "Text": "Check out our overview of Knowledge Anywhere\u0027s integration benefits and capabilities.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Single Sign-On",
      "Anchor": "single-sign-on",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Integration Overview",
        "Single Sign-On"
      ],
      "Text": "During the initial configuration, you can configure LinkedIn Learning and\nKnowledge Anywhere to establish a secure SAML single sign-on (SSO) connection to\nensure seamless access to content. SSO authentication reduces friction for users and administrators by eliminating the\nneed for manual user registration. SSO ensures learners spend more of their time watching content and less of their time trying to remember usernames and passwords.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Automated Content Catalog Sync",
      "Anchor": "automated-content-catalog-sync",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Integration Overview",
        "Automated Content Catalog Sync"
      ],
      "Text": "The LinkedIn Learning library contains thousands of courses. LinkedIn Learning\nadds courses at a rate of 20-30 per week at no extra cost. The Knowledge\nAnywhere administrator manually uploads new content at regular intervals.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Automated Content Catalog Sync",
      "Anchor": "automated-content-catalog-sync",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Integration Overview",
        "Automated Content Catalog Sync"
      ],
      "Text": "The Knowledge Anywhere deep integration with LinkedIn Learning uses LinkedIn\nLearning APIs to daily refresh the content library. This feature ensures\nLinkedIn Learning makes new content available within 24 hours of release.\nLinkedIn Learning aggregates and indexes all content titles and descriptions to\naccommodate keyword searches and support efficient discoverability. Knowledge\nAnywhere supports automatic syncing of English only content libraries.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Enabling SAML SSO",
      "Anchor": "enabling-saml-sso",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Integration Overview",
        "Enabling SAML SSO"
      ],
      "Text": "We recommend SAML SSO for all enterprise learning platform integrations. You can configure SSO\nauthentication in your LinkedIn Learning Admin settings. Most\norganizations have a centrally-managed identity management solution like Azure\nAD, Okta, or ADFS that you can configure to authenticate users into enterprise\napplications like LinkedIn Learning.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Enabling SAML SSO",
      "Anchor": "enabling-saml-sso",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Integration Overview",
        "Enabling SAML SSO"
      ],
      "Text": "To configure SAML SSO with your identity management solution, review the LinkedIn Learning SSO Implementation Guide.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Provision API Keys for Content Catalog Sync",
      "Anchor": "provision-api-keys-for-content-catalog-sync",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Configuration",
        "Provision API Keys for Content Catalog Sync"
      ],
      "Text": "For Knowledge Anywhere to sync LinkedIn Learning catalog metadata, API keys must be provisioned in LinkedIn Learning admin settings.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Provision API Keys for Content Catalog Sync",
      "Anchor": "provision-api-keys-for-content-catalog-sync",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Configuration",
        "Provision API Keys for Content Catalog Sync"
      ],
      "Text": "After you log in, if you are not already in the Admin screen, select Go to Admin.\n\n\n\nFrom the side navigation menu, select Access content and reports via API and expand Generate LinkedIn Learning REST API Application.\n\nSelect API Application Provision.\n\nClick Add application.\n\nIn the Add LinkedIn Learning API application screen, enter \u0022Knowledge Anywhere\u0022 in the Application Name field.\n\nIn the Application description field, provide a short description of the integration use case. For example, \u0022Knowledge Anywhere content catalog sync\u0022.\n\nUnder Choose keys, there are two checkboxes \u2013 Content and Report. Select\u00A0Content.\u202F\u00A0\n\nClick Next and accept the \u0022Terms and Conditions\u0022.\n\n\n\n\n\nCopy the Client ID and Client Secret in the LinkedIn Learning App configuration into the corresponding Knowledge Anywhere fields.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Knowledge Anywhere Configuration",
      "Anchor": "knowledge-anywhere-configuration",
